OL,3,ABBC apologises for 'any offence caused'
OL,4,Aby Strictly noise disruption
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC has apologised "for any offence
OL,7,Fcaused" after lewd audio was heard
OL,8,Fduring the live broadcast of Strictly
OL,9,FCome Dancing.
OL,11,FA recording of sex noises appeared to
OL,12,Fbe playing from the audience in
OL,13,FBlackpool's Tower Ballroom as judge
OL,14,FMotsi Mabuse gave feedback early in
OL,15,FSaturday's episode. She paused before
OL,16,Fjoking: "It's not me."
OL,23,APub: 22-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG6/38
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
